IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp5-months`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, RELATED PROVISIONS (lines 3138 to 3296 of the Act file): transitional and savings provisions of
-- amending Acts, shown for information. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Two of them still decide something for a person and are encoded here:
--   * 2004, c. 22, s. 23: section 70.1 (reinstatement) does not reach a person who stopped receiving a disability pension
--     because of returning to work before section 20 of that Act came into force;
--   * 2007, c. 11, s. 36: when subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) applies to an application for a disability pension.
-- The days on which those sections of the amending Acts came into force are not in the text: they are stated inputs.
-- Every other related provision is inert (NOTES.md, coverage table): the 2003 transfer of securities, the 2008 remittance
-- dates, the 2012 transition to the Social Security Tribunal (spent by its own dates of 1 April 2013 and 31 March 2014), the
-- 2016 costs of administration, and the "subsection 114(2) does not apply" and "order in council" commencement provisions.

§ `Related provisions that still decide something`

§§ `2004, c. 22, s. 23 -- section 70.1 does not apply to those who returned to work before section 20 came into force`

-- src:3149 | — 2004, c. 22, s. 23
-- src:3151 | 23 Section 70.1 of the Canada Pension Plan, as enacted by section 20 of this Act, does not apply in respect of persons who, before the coming into force of section 20 of this Act, have ceased to receive a disability pension because they have returned to work.
@ref Act Related Provisions, 2004, c. 22, s. 23 (src:3151)
GIVEN `the person ceased to receive a disability pension because they returned to work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` IS A DATE
      `day section 20 of the 2004 Act came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`RP 2004 c. 22 s 23 — section 70.1 does not apply in respect of the person` `the person ceased to receive a disability pension because they returned to work` `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` `day section 20 of the 2004 Act came into force` MEANS
        `the person ceased to receive a disability pension because they returned to work`
    AND `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` BELOW `day section 20 of the 2004 Act came into force`

§§ `2007, c. 11, s. 36 -- when subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) applies`

-- src:3153 | — 2007, c. 11, s. 36
-- src:3155 | 36 (1) Subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) of the Canada Pension Plan, as enacted by section 2, applies in respect of an application for a disability pension made in or after the month in which that section comes into force.
-- src:3156 | Limitation
-- src:3157 | (2) However, in the case of a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii) of the Canada Pension Plan, subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) of that Act, as enacted by section 2, applies only if the contributor is deemed to have become disabled no earlier than 15 months before the month in which that section comes into force.
@ref Act Related Provisions, 2007, c. 11, s. 36 (src:3155-3157)
GIVEN `a day in the month the application for a disability pension was made` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month section 2 of the 2007 Act came into force` IS A DATE
      `the contributor is a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`RP 2007 c. 11 s 36 — subparagraph 44(2)(a)(i.1) applies in respect of the application` `a day in the month the application for a disability pension was made` `a day in the month section 2 of the 2007 Act came into force` `the contributor is a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii)` `a day in the month the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` MEANS
    -- (1) an application made in or after the month in which the section comes into force
        `the month of a date` `a day in the month the application for a disability pension was made` AT LEAST `the month of a date` `a day in the month section 2 of the 2007 Act came into force`
    -- (2) in the case of a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii), only if deemed to have become disabled no earlier
    --     than 15 months before the month in which the section comes into force
    AND (   (NOT `the contributor is a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii)`)
         OR `the month of a date` `a day in the month the contributor is deemed to have become disabled` AT LEAST `cp5 helper -- the month a number of months from the month of a date` `a day in the month section 2 of the 2007 Act came into force` (0 MINUS 15))
